WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.740
"John Wick Chapter 4" isn't over by the&nbsp;
time the credits start rolling. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.285
the post-credits scene might just hint&nbsp;
toward the future of the franchise.

00:00:08.285 --> 00:00:10.706
Spoilers for John Wick 4.

00:00:10.706 --> 00:00:16.260
After four films, five dogs, and a handful of&nbsp;
High Table seats being vacated, the Baba Yaga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:22.020
finally bit the dust in "John Wick: Chapter 4."&nbsp;
Parking himself on the stone steps all bloodied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:27.060
and beaten, he calls out his wife's name and,&nbsp;
seemingly, shuffles off this mortal coil. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.860
while the world may have lost John Wick, the&nbsp;
assassins network and the allies or enemies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.480
inhabiting it are still in business, as are&nbsp;
scores that desperately need to be settled.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.120
One such feud that spills over following&nbsp;
John's Parisian-based payback is between Akira,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.160
and the former friend of Koji's that killed&nbsp;
him, Caine. In fact, their dispute is so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.060
significant it got its own bit of screen&nbsp;
time in a post-credit scene of "John Wick:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.858
Chapter 4," marking a first for the&nbsp;
film series that we didn't expect.

00:00:54.858 --> 00:00:59.880
But what does this sliver of a showdown imply for&nbsp;
a franchise's future that, as far as we know now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.642
is without its firearm-loving frontman?&nbsp;
Here's where the series could go next.

00:01:04.642 --> 00:01:07.075
"What did you think was going to happen?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.075 --> 00:01:12.420
What did you expect? Huh? Did you really&nbsp;
think this day was never going to come?"

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.580
Following the bloodbath at The Continental&nbsp;
Osaka, which saw Caine cut down Koji,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.960
Akira swears revenge against her father's&nbsp;
killer and isn't seen again for the rest of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.220
the film. It's not like Caine is keen to do it,&nbsp;
of course, given that he's under orders to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.480
John down along with anyone else helping him for&nbsp;
fear of his own daughter being killed should he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.413
fail to do so. It is in the post-credit scene&nbsp;
that we finally see Akira go in for the kill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.413 --> 00:01:40.633
hoping to get blood for blood, until a swift cut&nbsp;
to black stops us from witnessing the outcome.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:45.420
It's an unexpected extra to the story not just&nbsp;
because it follows the climax of John Wick's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:50.160
journey, but because it's teasing a spin-off&nbsp;
that isn't either of the two already confirmed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.960
Ana De Armas' "Ballerina" and the TV prequel&nbsp;
show, "The Continental," have been well-known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.476
projects in development for some time and we&nbsp;
haven't caught a glimpse of either so far.

00:01:59.476 --> 00:02:03.900
With that in mind, hinting at another area for&nbsp;
the burgeoning franchise to expand with this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:09.060
plotline is a welcome surprise. For starters, it&nbsp;
means more tales to tell in this world of markers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.800
trackers, and tailored bulletproof suits, but&nbsp;
also, given the characters and story involved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.700
this could end up being a "John Wick" spin-off&nbsp;
movie the franchise didn't know it needed.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.380
Since the beginning, John Wick, for the most&nbsp;
part, has been a lone wolf, only showing us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:27.120
one side of a story and teaming up with other&nbsp;
gunslingers for relatively brief scenes, both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.820
in "Parabellum" with Halle Berry and Lance Reddick&nbsp;
and in "Chapter 4" with Donnie Yen. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:37.680
these were highlights in both films and a&nbsp;
stylistic choice that could be replicated in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.660
future movie with Donnie Yen and Rina Sawayama&nbsp;
in a more detailed fashion. Not only could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.920
this potential project tell a complicated story&nbsp;
that pits two compelling characters against one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.120
another, but it could also see them working&nbsp;
together as a team when the dust settles.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.740
We know that Caine isn't a bad guy, and the&nbsp;
actions taken against Akira's family were to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.180
protect his own. This could be the murky middle&nbsp;
ground the potential enemies could meet on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.093
just like Caine and Wick did, leaving&nbsp;
them to unite and go after the High Table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.093 --> 00:03:08.640
the powers that make this world as cruel&nbsp;
and cold-hearted as it is. Sure, Marquis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.260
de Gramont may be out of the picture, but when it&nbsp;
comes to that mysterious organization, that's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:18.267
table that has plenty more room to clear. Akira,&nbsp;
along with Caine, could be the ones to do it.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:22.200
Should they be successful, from there they&nbsp;
could branch off into their own solo films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.920
expanding on a world that has so much&nbsp;
more potential and, more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.000
so many more killer contracts to be&nbsp;
completed. After all, we're still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.228
waiting to see if we ever see Jason Mantzoukas'&nbsp;
unforgettable Tick-Tock Man back on screen.

00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:37.782
"Tick tock Mr. Wick. Tick tock."

